# Line endings must be DETERMINISTIC, because the build hashes file contents.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. scripts/build-dist.js keeps an immutable-cache lock: it
# records a hash of every asset served under a URL with no ?v= cache-buster, and
# fails the build if one changes content without changing URL. /Assets/* is served
# `immutable, max-age=31536000`, so that guard is the only thing standing between
# a silent edit and a year of stale bytes in every visitor's cache.
#
# The repo had no .gitattributes and the machine has core.autocrlf=true, so a text
# file's bytes depended on WHERE it was checked out. Measured 2026-08-01 on
# Assets/brand/integrations/color-okta.svg:
#
#   working tree   274 bytes, LF    -> a78ee153dd5bab3a
#   fresh clone    275 bytes, CRLF  -> 825a0974fa5ce494
#
# One byte of line ending, a different hash, and therefore a different verdict from
# the guard depending on the checkout. Recording the lock from a CRLF-free working
# tree made every fresh clone disagree with it, which is exactly what Cloudflare
# Pages does on every build. Four consecutive deploys failed on that guard and the
# site sat on a broken stylesheet while the pushes appeared to succeed.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the working tree match the repository on every platform, so a hash
# recorded here is the hash Cloudflare computes. Do not remove this without also
# removing the content-hash guard, and prefer keeping the guard.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary: never touch these, and do not try to diff them as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
